.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd July 31, 2026
.Dt AUDITBROKERD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm auditbrokerd
.Nd authenticated BSM audit broker
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
provides the global
.Dq system.Audit
service from
.Pa /Capabilities/System/Audit.cap .
It runs as root because
.Xr audit 2
requires
.Dv PRIV_AUDIT_SUBMIT .
It cannot run in a jail because the kernel rejects audit submission from
jailed credentials.
Each client receives a capability-mode worker which prohibits fork, IPC,
incoming descriptor transfer, exec, and new sockets.
The supervisor retains each worker's process descriptor, observes exit through
.Dv EVFILT_PROCDESC ,
and admits at most 4096 concurrent workers.  On managed quiesce it first stops
admission, terminates and reaps every worker, and only then acknowledges
shutdown to
.Xr serviced 8 .
.Pp
The serviced-authenticated provider identity selects a fixed BSM event.
Requests cannot choose an event number, audit user ID, or provider identity.
Only the built-in FileSystemCmp, NetworkCmp, LogCmp, and Notify identities
are accepted.
Each session is rate limited to a burst of 200 records and 100 records per
second.
.Sh SECURITY
.Nm
exists so functional components do not need root merely to produce trusted
audit records.
Subject and operation fields have fixed bounds and a restricted character
set.
Unknown providers are rejected before a worker is created.
The
.Xr audit 2
system call is capability-mode enabled but retains its root privilege check
and jail prohibition.
.Sh OBSERVABILITY
The
.Dq auditcmpd
DTrace provider exports
.Sy session ,
.Sy submit ,
and
.Sy reject
probes.
They report the authenticated provider label, selected fixed event, submitted
error value, and operation result without exposing an arbitrary audit record.
Submission and rejection outcomes are also represented by the broker's BSM
records where a record can be submitted safely.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr audit 2 ,
.Xr libauditcmp 3 ,
.Xr libservice 3
